#!/bin/bash
# t2-start.sh (2026-11-02): start of the turn, through the front door: the hydration as it stands, the owner's design words of this turn
# ingested, and the checkpoints they ask for added to the cortex outline.
export PATH=$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH
echo "=== hydrate cortex (start of turn)"; cortex hydrate cortex 2>&1 | head -6; echo "..."
echo "=== owner's words of this turn, ingested"
cortex ingest cortex "owner 2026-11-02: jev does yes or no, probability as a multiple choice, a confidence score, a probabilistic boolean, and batching; it is fast because it does all of it deterministically and you choose the output shape."
cortex ingest cortex "owner 2026-11-02: if you build it as a traditional llm you will build a classifier; they are too slow, we already tried. the nli failed before on two reasons: the context flood of llm context landing from six llms, the chunker could not keep up, and the classifier could not work fast enough to give hydrate the new state before the next call."
cortex ingest cortex "owner 2026-11-02: my system was a live adjusted weight system that back props live against a small selected corpus that changes, so the model weights change over state and time, and the weights are only used over categoric uses; the corpus of the model is only the corpus it needs to solve the problem."
cortex ingest cortex "owner 2026-11-02: the model is not designed to talk to humans; it is designed to answer decide, compare, invent, guess, wild ass guess very fast; it does not decide the truth, it decides the confidence of the current state versus the prior state."
cortex ingest cortex "owner 2026-11-02: if the guessing is built as its own state it is another neuron brain taught to be the guessing brain; hc would have to exist, as does the process for a temporary corpus and a corpus store so it can recall temporary corpuses and improve back prop times; it switches corpuses very fast, heartbeat to heartbeat."
cortex ingest cortex "owner 2026-11-02: new state is not defined completely by new ingest; new state is defined slowly over time; accept the parts that improve the state and reject the dupes or degressions; it is not all or nothing."
cortex ingest cortex "owner 2026-11-02: there has to be a filter for everything that comes in: tool calls, loading scripts, the non important chunks; it is delivered as a context whole and then checked line by line, live delete of lines that are duped or restated, so the corpus ingest shrinks to only the information pertaining to the state it is reasoning over, and nothing of the tool calls bloats the db."
cortex ingest cortex "owner 2026-11-02: a brain with a slow build time and a deterministic runtime is the answer; many processes each a microsecond or two, each filling a cell of the run data sheet; once the sheet is full of state, memories, sources, current state, ingest state, previous known drift, invention fails and successes, pattern matching, the substitution formulas fire and complete the diff, contra, reasoning, drift and meaning checks to perform the output; in a specific order; no timers, chunkers, walkers, sweeps."
echo "=== new checkpoints from these words"
cortex checkpoint cortex 10 : "the ingest filter: every ingest is a context whole checked line by line; duped, restated and noise lines (tool calls, scripts, paths, code) are dropped live before anything is typed; the counts are reported" "||" "a messy worker output with repeated, restated and tool-call lines is ingested and only the pertaining sentences reach the brain, the dropped lines counted by reason, in milliseconds"
cortex checkpoint cortex 11 : "the judge as a run data sheet: deterministic cells first (dupe, restated, noise, words shared with scope and expected, geometry, the worker's own expected mark, this project's past drift and invention counts), then the judgment cells from jev when a key exists, then the formulas that give the verdict" "||" "a verdict line carries its whole sheet; the deterministic cells alone settle dupe, restated, noise and off-scope; completes and progresses stay unsettled until a judgment cell is filled"
cortex checkpoint cortex 12 : "part-wise state: a checkpoint's accepted state is the set of sentences accepted into it over time; a verdict of completes, progresses or supersedes accepts the sentence as a part; dupes tick; degressions are rejected; the hydration shows the accepted parts" "||" "cortex accept <name> <n> <run> adds a part; the hydration lists the parts; a repeat of an accepted part ticks and is not added twice"
cortex checkpoint cortex 13 : "the guessing brain design in the owner's words recorded for the neuron project: a second brain taught to guess, with hc, a temporary corpus and a corpus store, live back propagation over a small selected corpus, output as decide, compare, invent, guess, wild guess with confidence" "||" "the neuron project's hydration carries the guessing brain's design lines; nothing is built until the owner says so"
cortex state cortex 10 working
echo "=== hydrate cortex again: what the brain says is next"; cortex hydrate cortex 2>&1 | sed -n 2,4p
